<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys 32,000T Jan jet fuel at around $270/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys 32,000T Jan jet fuel at around $270/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp has bought by tender a 32,000-tonne jet fuel cargo for arrival in the second half of January, a company source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The cargo was awarded at around $270 per tonne for delivery to Keelung or Shen Ao on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis, the source said.</p>
<p>Traders said the cargo was awarded to Swiss trader Glencore but this was not confirmed.</p>
<p>The tender closed on December 10 and offers were valid until December 12.  </p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC bought two 32,000-tonne cargoes for second-half December arrival at around $241-242 per tonne, c-and-f basis.</p>
<p>Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
